    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d819">

                <pb facs="1109" n="973" sameAs="frus:frus1929v01/pg973"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">714.1515/982: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Guatemala</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Hawks</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-11-28T10:00:00-06:00">November 28, 1929—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 5:30 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>154. Referring to the Department’s telegram of November 27, 2 p.m.<anchor n="45"
                        xml:id="d819-f1"/> The Minister for Foreign Affairs still maintains the
                    position that unless the Government of Honduras makes the same clear cut
                    statement without any reservations, as has already been made by the Guatemalan
                    Government, to the effect that its delegate will be able to discuss all phases
                    of the problem it will be useless to hold the conference.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Honduras.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hawks</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d819-f1" n="45" xml:id="d819-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; it requested the Chargé to inquire whether it would be satisfactory
                    to the Guatemalan Government to have the delegates meet at Washington on January
                    15, 1930. (714.1515/973)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
